        <mxCell id="trace" value="&lt;b&gt;External TEDM trace package (not native DAO-ML)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;CG/AR/CP/M/ER records preserve rationales, rejected alternatives, thresholds, baselines, residual risks, and cross-model links. Key review chains: ER1→AR1/CP4/M3; ER2→AR2/CP5/M4; ER3→AR3–AR5/CP3–CP4/M2–M3/M6; ER4→AR3/TP3–TP4/CP1–CP2/CP6/M1/M5–M6." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;align=left;spacing=10;fontSize=14;dashed=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="320" y="1450" width="3340" height="150" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gates" value="&lt;b&gt;Sowelu review gates&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Confirm whether each authority is a Role or Committee. 2. Split permission sets into the preferred individual DAO-ML glyphs. 3. Confirm associated_to endpoints. 4. Confirm that each is_controlled_by edge really denotes assignment/revocation or permission delegation—not ownership or oversight. 5. Fix appointment methods, committee bounds, signer independence/threshold, veto, emergency scope/expiry, and audit ownership. 6. Run XSD plus XPath validation." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;align=left;spacing=10;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="320" y="1660" width="3340" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

